1. Work performed: Added the monolithic include, env gate, descriptor-upload helpers, and the new `Impl` members in [expert_layer.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/expert_layer.cpp#L496) and [expert_layer.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/expert_layer.cpp#L678). In `ExpertLayerSlice::Create()`, direct-MLP layers now try monolithic routed-expert residency first, build both monolithic and routed device-side `FusedNvfp4WeightView` arrays from the contiguous buffers, set `monolithic_resident`, and skip the old per-expert residency loop when that succeeds; the fallback path remains unchanged when monolithic is disabled or fails at [expert_layer.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/expert_layer.cpp#L1040). I also added the requested debug line and `valid()` checks for monolithic residency at [expert_layer.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/expert_layer.cpp#L1306) and [expert_layer.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/expert_layer.cpp#L1385).

2. How monolithic upload extracts data from `GemmDescriptor`: the upload helper reads the host-backed `descriptor.packed_data` and `descriptor.packed_nbytes` for packed FP4 bytes, `descriptor.block_scales_data` and `descriptor.block_scales_nbytes` for the raw row-major block scales, and `descriptor.tensor_scale_data` reinterpreted as a `const float*` after checking `tensor_scale_nbytes == sizeof(float)` at [expert_layer.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/expert_layer.cpp#L501). Those exact raw descriptor pointers are then passed into `MonolithicNvfp4ExpertWeights::UploadExpert()` at [expert_layer.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/expert_layer.cpp#L509).

